<title>ZIMBABWE: Clan raises yr shr, sees better 1997.</title>
<headline>Clan raises yr shr, sees better 1997.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year results to Dec 31</p>
<p>(all figures in million Z$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr	    44.0  cts vs  32.0 cts</p>
<p>    Div	    17.0  cts vs  11.0 cts</p>
<p>    Pre-tax	23.78     vs  17.87</p>
<p>    Tax	     7.93     vs   6.35</p>
<p>    After-tax    15.85     vs  11.52</p>
<p>    Turnover    156.02     vs 126.32</p>
<p>Div payable April 24</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Clan Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Note - The group said that 1997 would bring it further growth and increased earnings because of an economy that was expected to be more resilient due to good rains.</p>
<p>It said turnover was forecast to reach Z$200 million. It said attributable earnings were expected to be in the region of Z$20 million, equating to an earnings per share figure of 55 cents.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
</text>
